34, 874, 37734, 13, 12674, 25, 2857, 25748, 4175, 48530, 11039, 26849, 37734, 13, 4866, 1906, 30, 5805, 2336, 30942, 5940, 20218, 6679, 26887, 2586, 25, 2469, 1179, 803, 13, 1987, 2407, 25, 5046, 2256, 3147, 1076, 2129, 591, 3147, 1076, 8934, 59, 77, 13, 14235, 20480, 13, 1368, 567, 958, 2857, 36037, 321, 288, 3937, 11, 874, 37734, 13, 14235, 2426, 18922, 13, 16018, 958, 2857, 6899, 19314, 3501, 553, 31462, 303, 3165, 5202, 30, 1921, 364, 5787, 3889, 13514, 6891, 5639, 874, 8615, 10487, 13, 1368, 567, 1791, 3165, 5202, 421, 7062, 8615, 10487, 321, 3107, 2458, 11, 1412, 12497, 1000, 2222, 318, 2674, 10487, 3568, 321, 37734, 553, 14235, 524, 2222, 8976, 7465, 13, 1987, 1412, 14090, 1902, 6922, 6891, 5639, 1973, 8615, 10487, 321, 874, 37734, 13, 12674, 1965, 1902, 716, 8615, 10487, 321, 958, 53265, 310, 884, 37734, 13, 16018, 599, 12755, 3165, 1401, 3501, 11], "content": "We need answer user's request. Need refactor Go HTTP handler into testable functions with clear error handling, keep external behavior identical (same status codes, same response bodies). Return full refactored file, then list behaviors unit test should cover.\n\nNeed think carefully. Original code:\npackage main\nimport database/sql, encoding/json, net/http, strconv\nvar db *sql.DB\nfunc userHandler(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n idStr := r.URL.Query().Get(\"id\")\n id, err := strconv.Atoi(idStr)\n if err != nil || id <= 0 {\n  w.WriteHeader(400)\n  w.Write([]byte(`{\"error\":\"bad id\"}`))\n  return\n }\n row := db.QueryRow(\"SELECT name, email FROM users WHERE id = ?\", id)\n var name, email string\n if err := row.Scan(&name, &email); err != nil {\n  if err == sql.ErrNoRows {\n   w.WriteHeader(404)\n   w.Write([]byte(`{\"error\":\"not found\"}`))\n   return\n  }\n  w.WriteHeader(500)\n  w.Write([]byte(`{\"error\":\"db\"}`))\n  return\n }\n w.Header().Set(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n json.NewEncoder(w).Encode(map[string]string{\"name\": name, \"email\": email})\n}\n\nNeed refactor: separate database access, input validation, JSON encoding into testable functions with clear error handling. Keep external behavior identical: same status codes, same response bodies. Important: original success response: Content-Type set after possible errors? For errors, no Content-Type set. Body exactly {\"error\":\"bad id\"} no newline. Success: json.Encoder.Encode adds trailing newline. Map order? Go map marshaling sorts keys alphabetically: email then name. So body: {\"email\":\"...\",\"name\":\"...\"}\\n. Need preserve. If we use json.Marshal and w.Write, no newline. Need keep identical. Could use json.NewEncoder(w).Encode in writeJSON? But for errors original writes raw bytes no Content-Type. If we create writeJSON that sets Content-Type and encodes, error bodies would change (Content-Type added and newline). Need not change external behavior. So error responses must remain raw bytes without Content-Type and no newline. Success response must set Content-Type and use Encoder to add newline. Could have helper writeError(w,", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0030493689700961113], [760, -6.889895915985107]], [[1144, -1.180178969661938e-05], [14235, -12.023780822753906]], [[4087, -0.008742408826947212], [310, -4.979012489318848]], [[1156, -0.036104463040828705], [303, -3.6577093601226807]], [[579, -0.21355722844600677], [25, -2.361201286315918]], [[1622, -0.0036113422829657793], [3296, -6.444079399108887]], [[13, -0.365129679441452], [25, -1.4968740940093994]], [[14235, -0.034766118973493576], [1165, -4.099452018737793]], [[89109, -0.3547886312007904], [7936, -1.7281559705734253]], [[5805, -0.00023397560289595276], [2400, -8.750519752502441]], [[9830, -0.02595438063144684], [6795, -3.712618827819824]], [[6795, -3.1352534278994426e-05], [17369, -11.790610313415527]], [[1083, -1.3992794752120972], [47781, -1.6043843030929565]], [[1228, -0.09465399384498596], [2400, -2.8386783599853516]], [[470, -3.242545426473953e-05], [5568, -10.602516174316406]], [[5568, -0.003153463